*.so

# Distribution / packaging
.Python
build/
develop-eggs/
dist/
downloads/
eggs/
.eggs/
# `lib/` is a Python build artifact (pip's `--target`, `build/lib`). It was written unanchored,
# so it also swallowed `frontend/js/lib/` — the three modules that own the window's bridge, DOM
# helpers and event feed were never tracked, while `frontend/bundle.js` (generated from them)
# was. A clean clone would have lost the source and the window would still have worked, which
# is the worst version of that bug. Anchoring the rule to the repository root is the fix that
# does not need an exception: a `!dir/` rule cannot re-include anything, because git never
# descends into an ignored directory.
/lib/
/lib64/
parts/
sdist/
var/
wheels/
pip-wheel-metadata/
share/python-wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg
MANIFEST

# PyInstaller
